 4.12126C18.6834 3.73074 19.3166 3.73074 19.7071 4.12126L19.8787 4.29283C20.2692 4.68336 20.2692 5.31653 19.8787 5.70705L18.8622 6.72357L17.3068 5.10738L18.2929 4.12126ZM15.8923 6.52185L17.4477 8.13804L10.4888 15.097L8.37437 15.6256L8.90296 13.5112L15.8923 6.52185ZM4 7.99994C4 7.44766 4.44772 6.99994 5 6.99994H10C10.5523 6.99994 11 6.55223 11 5.99994C11 5.44766 10.5523 4.99994 10 4.99994H5C3.34315 4.99994 2 6.34309 2 7.99994V18.9999C2 20.6568 3.34315 21.9999 5 21.9999H16C17.6569 21.9999 19 20.6568 19 18.9999V13.9999C19 13.4477 18.5523 12.9999 18 12.9999C17.4477 12.9999 17 13.4477 17 13.9999V18.9999C17 19.5522 16.5523 19.9999 16 19.9999H5C4.44772 19.9999 4 19.5522 4 18.9999V7.99994Z\" fill=\"#currentColor\" class=\"svelte-e3bi7l\"></path>\n      </svg> \n      <!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!--[!--><!--]--><!----></a>\n    </div>\n   </div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"tabs grit\">\n   <a data-sveltekit-noscroll=\"\" href=\"https://syntax.fm/show/1042/is-the-jev-hype-overblown\" class=\"active\">Show Notes</a> <a data-sveltekit-noscroll=\"\" href=\"https://syntax.fm/show/1042/is-the-jev-hype-overblown/transcript\">Transcript</a><!---->\n  </div>\n  <!---->\n  <section class=\"layout full\">\n   <!---->\n   <div class=\"main\">\n    <div class=\"show-notes\">\n     <!---->\n     <p>Is Jev actually a leap forward for classification or just hype and fake demos? We dig in, plus Claude Code's new AGENTS.md support, TinyCast (the free, open-source Raycast alternative), an iPhone Fold simulator in Xcode, and a stack of dev tools you'll want to try</p>\n     <h3 id=\"show-notes\">Show Notes</h3>\n     <ul>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=00:00\">00:00</a></strong> Welcome to Syntax!</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=01:17\">01:17</a></strong> The iPhone Fold Simulator and Foldable Web APIs\n       <ul>\n        <li><a href=\"https://bsky.app/profile/bram.us/post/3mvx3tcoa3c2c\">Features behind a flag</a></li>\n        <li><a href=\"https://syntax.fm/meetup\">Syntax Meetup in San Francisco</a></li>\n       </ul></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=07:03\">07:03</a></strong> Claude Code Finally Supports <a href=\"https://x.com/trq212/status/2101009392611278961\">agents.md</a>\n       <ul>\n        <li><a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\">Changelog</a></li>\n       </ul></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=11:42\">11:42</a></strong> Using Your Claude Subscription Inside PI</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=13:07\">13:07</a></strong> Raycast Pricing Changes and the Rise of <a href=\"https://tinycast.dev/\">Tinycast</a></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=18:24\">18:24</a></strong> Our Most Used Raycast Features</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=21:22\">21:22</a></strong> Browser Hopping: Back on Helium After Ditching Dia</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=22:12\">22:12</a></strong> 1Password's Redesign and Reliability Problems</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=23:11\">23:11</a></strong> <a href=\"https://typesafe.ai/blog/introducing-system-one-models-and-jev\">Jev Explained: A Model That Only Answers Questions</a></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=31:59\">31:59</a></strong> CJ's Jev Chat Bot Demo With MCP Tools</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=36:09\">36:09</a></strong> The Kevs in the Room: Open Source Jev Alternatives\n       <ul>\n        <li><a href=\"https://x.com/michellechen/status/2101091012559151480\">Cloudflare’s Kev</a></li>\n        <li><a href=\"https://github.com/jaredpalmer/kev/tree/main\">Jared Palmer’s Kev</a></li>\n       </ul></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=45:39\">45:39</a></strong> What We've Actually Built With Jev So Far\n       <ul>\n        <li><a href=\"https://benchmarkheaven.com/jev-models\">Jev Benchmarks</a></li>\n       </ul></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=51:59\">51:59</a></strong> Brought to you by <a href=\"https://sentry.io/syntax\">Sentry.io</a></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=52:55\">52:55</a></strong> <a href=\"https://gpui-kit.com/\">GPUI Kit</a>: Building Native Rust Desktop Apps</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=58:07\">58:07</a></strong> <a href=\"https://devfra.me/posts/pluggable-extensible-playful-devtools\">Antfu's DevFrame: A Framework for Building Dev Tools</a></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=59:45\">59:45</a></strong> Where Is the Line on Using AI in Video Editing?\n       <ul>\n        <li><a href=\"https://x.com/runwayml/status/2100620377005203564\">Runwayml Upscaling</a></li>\n       </ul></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=01:06:00\">01:06:00</a></strong> AI Upscaled Security Photos and Internet Detectives</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=01:08:07\">01:08:07</a></strong> <a href=\"https://qwen.ai/blog?id=qwen-image-2.1\">Qwen Image 2.1</a> and Real Transparent Backgrounds</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=01:10:18\">01:10:18</a></strong> <a href=\"https://john.hartnup.uk/2026/06/07/ai-event-posters.html\">AI Generated Posters Don't Have to Be Horrible</a></li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=01:13:28\">01:13:28</a></strong> <a href=\"https://www.onorca.dev/\">Orca</a>: A GUI for Wrangling Your Fleet of Agents</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=01:15:37\">01:15:37</a></strong> Grok 4.7 First Impressions and Its Pricing</li>\n      <li><strong><a href=\"#t=01:18:58\">01:18:58</a></strong> Waiting on Google and Microsoft's Big Models</li>\n     </ul>\n     <h3 id=\"hit-us-up-on-socials\">Hit us up on Socials!</h3>\n     <p>Syntax: <a href=\"https://twitter.com/syntaxfm\">X</a> <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/syntax_fm/\">Instagram</a> <a href=\"https://www.tiktok.com/@syntaxfm\">Tiktok</a> <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/96077407/admin/feed/posts/\">LinkedIn</a> <a href=\"https://www.threads.net/@syntax_fm\">Threads</a></p>\n     <p>Wes: <a href=\"https